From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: chromium-blink-ios <noreply@github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] iOS Curium: scroll the page under floating top controls

Keep the UIKit viewport fixed and let Blink and cc consume scroll delta for
the top browser controls. Viz embeds the page at the offset carried by the
frame it draws and records that offset when the frame is presented. Native
input and selection map through the presented offset. A pinch keeps its
native point for cc, which anchors zoom with its live offset; hit tests and
the synthetic Ctrl-wheel of a touchpad pinch use page space.

Keep the full-size widget and update the band height with the viewport.
Allow gesture reveals only at page top, including while settling. Commit
the ratio of a new document, of a history load and of a restored scroll in
place of compositor deltas and animations. Account for the band when
revealing a focused field, and retain the ratio through DOM fullscreen.

